uilt Website | Blink","url":"https://blink.new/p/inds-3d-website-gvvmmc4g#:~:text=developers","text":"developers.","pub_date":null,"extra":{"cited_message_idx":7,"cited_message_id":"06d82679-ba37-4d98-91ea-6f717cae20f1","search_result_idx":null,"evidence_text":"","start_line_num":169,"end_line_num":177,"connector_source":null},"og_tags":null}},{"start_ix":8092,"end_ix":8104,"citation_format_type":"tether_v4","metadata":{"type":"webpage","title":"WebGL, glTF, and X3D: The Three Pillars of Interactive 3D on the Web | Web3D Consortium","url":"https://www.web3d.org/blog/anitahavele/webgl-gltf-and-x3d-three-pillars-interactive-3d-web#:~:text=WebGL%3A%20The%20Rendering%20Workhorse","text":"WebGL: The Rendering Workhorse","pub_date":null,"extra":{"cited_message_idx":16,"cited_message_id":"c5d27a0e-0e4e-4a21-b993-eebee3bd200a","search_result_idx":null,"evidence_text":"","start_line_num":52,"end_line_num":61,"connector_source":null},"og_tags":null}},{"start_ix":8194,"end_ix":8206,"citation_format_type":"tether_v4","metadata":{"type":"webpage","title":"3D web design best practices: a complete guide to immersive web experiences in 2026 | Verox Studio","url":"https://www.veroxstudio.com/blog/3d-web-design-best-practices-a-complete-guide-to-immersive-web-experiences-in-2#:~:text=Three,level%20graphics%20programming","text":"Three.js remains the dominant JavaScript library for creating 3D web experiences in 2026. Its extensive documentation, active community, and cross-browser compatibility make it the首选 for developers and designers alike. Three.js handles the complex WebGL abstractions, allowing teams to focus on creative expression rather than low-level graphics programming.","pub_date":null,"extra":{"cited_message_idx":15,"cited_message_id":"d123ef7e-1362-4a19-bd1f-e5cbb245a4b4","search_result_idx":null,"evidence_text":"","start_line_num":78,"end_line_num":86,"connector_source":null},"og_tags":null}},{"start_ix":8411,"end_ix":8425,"citation_format_type":"tether_v4","metadata":{"type":"webpage","title":"Three.js vs Unity for Web | Comparison Guide 2026","url":"https://www.utsubo.com/blog/threejs-vs-unity-web-comparison#:~:text=Three.js%20shipped%20production,it%20as%20of%20early%202026","text":"Three.js shipped production-ready WebGPU support in r171 (September 2025). Zero configuration needed—import `WebGPURenderer` and go. All major browsers support it as of early 2026.","pub_date":null,"extra":{"cited_message_idx":38,"cited_message_id":"acd5fafd-d360-4fd2-87e5-d232ef8a34c1","search_result_idx":null,"evidence_text":"","start_line_num":208,"end_line_num":217,"connector_source":null},"og_tags":null}},{"start_ix":8501,"end_ix":8515,"citation_format_type":"tether_v4","metadata":{"type":"webpage","title":"Three.js vs Unity for Web | Comparison Guide 2026","url":"https://www.utsubo.com/blog/threejs-vs-unity-web-comparison#:~:text=Metric%20%20,15%E2%80%9345%20seconds","text":"Metric  | Three.js  | Unity WebGL --- | --- | --- Core engine  | 500 kB–1 MB gzipped  | 5–15 MB compressed (WASM + framework) Typical full project  | 2–5 MB (core + models)  | 15–50 MB (engine + data + assets) First meaningful paint  | 2–6 seconds  | 8–30 seconds Time to interactive  | <10 seconds  | 15–45 seconds","pub_date":null,"extra":{"cited_message_idx":38,"cited_message_id":"acd5fafd-d360-4fd2-87e5-d232ef8a34c1","search_result_idx":null,"evidence_text":"","start_line_num":170,"end_line_num":178,"connector_source":null},"og_tags":null}},{"start_ix":8622,"end_ix":8636,"citation_format_type":"tether_v4","metadata":{"type":"webpage","title":"Three.js vs Unity for Web | Comparison Guide 2026","url":"https://www.utsubo.com/blog/threejs-vs-unity-web-comparison#:~:text=Metric%20%20,15%E2%80%9345%20seconds","text":"Metric  | Three.js  | Unity WebGL --- | --- | --- Core engine  | 500 kB–1 MB gzipped  | 5–15 MB compressed (WASM + framework) Typical full project  | 2–5 MB (core + models)  | 15–50 MB (engine + data + assets) First meaningful paint  | 2–6 seconds  | 8–30 seconds Time to interactive  | <10 seconds  | 15–45 seconds","pub_date":null,"extra":{"cited_message_idx":38,"cited_message_id":"acd5fafd-d360-4fd2-87e5-d232ef8a34c1","search_result_idx":null,"evidence_text":"","start_line_num":170,"end_line_num":178,"connector_source":null},"og_tags":null}},{"start_ix":8636,"end_ix":8650,"citation_format_type":"tether_v4","metadata":{"type":"webpage","title":"Three.js vs Unity for Web | Comparison Guide 2026","url":"https://www.utsubo.com/blog/threejs-vs-unity-web-comparison#:~:text=Three,WASM%20engine%20before%20anything%20renders","text":"Three.js loads like a regular website—progressive, streamable, with assets fetched on demand. Unity WebGL requires downloading and decompiling the entire WASM engine before anything renders.","pub_date":null,"extra":{"cited_message_idx":38,"cited_message_id":"acd5fafd-d360-4fd2-87e5-d232ef8a34c1","search_result_idx":null,"evidence_text":"","start_line_num":178,"end_line_num":184,"connector_source":null},"og_tags":null}},{"start_ix":8714,"end_ix":8726,"citation_format_type":"tether_v4","metadata":{"type":"webpage","title":"WebGL, glTF, and X3D: The Three Pillars of Interactive 3D on the Web | Web3D Consortium","url":"https://www.web3d.org/blog/anitahavele/webgl-gltf-and-x3d-three-pillars-interactive-3d-web#:~:text=glTF%3A%20The%20%E2%80%9CJPEG%20of%203D%E2%80%9D","text":"glTF: The “JPEG of 3D”","pub_date":null,"extra":{"cited_message_idx":16,"cited_message_id":"c5d27a0e-0e4e-4a21-b993-eebee3bd200a","search_result_idx":null,"evidence_text":"","start_line_num":82,"end_line_num":90,"connector_source":null},"og_tags":null}},{"start_ix":8855,"end_ix":8867,"citation_format_type":"tether_v4","metadata":{"type":"webpage","title":"WebGL, glTF, and X3D: The Three Pillars of Interactive 3D on the Web | Web3D Consortium","url":"https://www.web3d.org/blog/anitahavele/webgl-gltf-and-x3d-three-pillars-interactive-3d-web#:~:text=glTF%3A%20The%20%E2%80%9CJPEG%20of%203D%E2%80%9D","text":"glTF: The “JPEG of 3D”","pub_date